out the new helm: helm of anti-magic.. and I must say that it was a
really painful thing to be wearing against all of those angels. The
angels cast that magic missile attack thing heaps, and anti-magic
resists it - which sometimes causes the helm to stun me... and because
of the unicorn horn nerf I couldn't always cure the stun condition, so
I was stumbling around like crazy, trying to kill these damn angels;
getting slammed by their magic-missile attack (which still does 50%
damage even with magic-resistance)... I used up one of my amulets of
life saving getting to the first altar... and the altar was neutral! A
devastating blow for a lawful samurai, with my helm of opposite
alignment at the ready... so I set off to the next altar, but didn't
make it. My one remaining amulet of life saving wasn't enough.

So the moral of this story is that the helm of anti-magic truly is a
less useful form of magic resistance (because of the stun, which is
exactly how I wanted it to be. I didn't want my new helm to become
standard ascension equipment); and that the astral plane can be quite
dangerous for characters that are not properly equipped.


